Fix off-by-one admitting limit+1 events per window

The length check used <=, so a limiter configured for N events admitted
N+1 before rejecting: the comparison ran against the deque size before
the current event was appended. Existing test_does_not_exceed_limit was
failing on this.

Also correct the clock rationale in the docstring. DST does not shift
time.time(), which returns UTC epoch seconds; the reason to stay on the
monotonic clock is unbounded NTP/manual/suspend-resume steps in either
direction.
